==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[fund]] [[deposited]] by a [[customer]] (the depositor) in a bank from which they can make [[withdrawal]]s.
# {{rfv-sense|lang=en}} The [[formal]] [[relationship]] established between the [[depositor]] and the bank.
#* {{quote-book|year=2006|title=Internet Banking and the Law in Europe |author=Apostolos Ath. Gkoutzinis  |page= |ISBN=1139458671 |passage=In practice, as far as '''bank account''' services and electronic transfers of funds are concerned, the institutional and operational structure of national banking and and payment systems does not guarantee that cross-border banking operations enjoy the same level of automation, standaridzation and low cost as purely domestic transactions. }}
#* {{quote-book|year=2009|title=Fundamentals of Offshore Banking: How to Open Accounts Almost Anywhere |author=Walter Tyndale -   |page= |ISBN=0557063264 |passage=In the United States, for example, owners of foreign '''bank accounts''' are required to notify the IRS of these accounts. }}
#* {{quote-book|year=2012 |title=Access to Cash Machines for Basic Bank Account Holders |author=Great Britain: Parliament: House of Commons: Treasury Committee  |page= |ISBN=0215047710 |passage=Lloyds TSB basic '''bank account''' customers can now use all cash machines across Lloyds Banking Group (which includes Halifax, Bank of Scotland and Cheltenham & Gloucester). }}
#* {{quote-book|year=2017|title=Financial Inclusion for Poverty Alleviation |author=Essam Yassin Mohammed & ‎Zenebe Bashaw Uraguchi  |page= |ISBN=1351595113 |passage=Could this possibly mean that the mobile '''bank account''' services have overcome these barriers for the users? }}
# {{rfv-sense|lang=en}} A [[statement]] [[summarizing]] [[credit]] and [[debit]] [[transaction]]s with the account; a [[bank statement]].
#* {{quote-book|year=2012 |title=Sage 50 Accounts For Dummies  |author=Jane Kelly  |page=264 |ISBN=111831123X |passage=Reconciling your '''bank accounts''' normally forms part of your monthly accounting routine. }}
#* {{quote-book|year=2013 - |title=Xero For Dummies |author=Heather Smith  |page= |ISBN= 1118572521|passage=The last bookkeeper sat down at her computer, opened up a Xero file, created some '''bank accounts''' with activated bank feeds, and reconciled the accounts in Xero. }}

